From 31af7dfff3de650e75fc8910558a432a2f7db507 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 09:50:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] qsa: STRATA_ATTN_VBATCH=1 issues the decode attention's V
 loads 8 cells at a time (opt-in, =4 four cells)

attn_chunk_body's value loop read one cell per iteration: srow[c], then that cell's V load, then its
12 fmaf, so a block paid one dependent load round trip per cell (64 per chunk; sm_86 SASS unrolls by 2
but keeps each cell's LDGs behind its own guard).  With the switch the loop takes 8 (or 4) cells per
step, as PR #540's pre-sm_75 kernel does: the group's srow values and V loads first, then each cell
folded into the 12 accumulators in ascending order with the same fmaf and the same V expression
(load_v1, moved out of the pre-sm_75 #if unchanged).  A group with a masked cell (page -1) breaks to
the scalar loop at that group, which skips masked cells as before (never folds them with weight 0:
fmaf(0, v, -0.0f) is +0.0f).  The tail (n_here not a multiple of the group) runs the scalar loop.

A template parameter VBATCH (0, 4, 8) on attn_chunk_body, attn_chunk_kernel and
attn_chunk_slots_kernel; the per-row batch launcher (warp and lane-cell scoring), the slots launcher
and qsa_decode_attn_step select it.  The pre-sm_75 / gfx103x kernel keeps precedence, the gfx906 query
swizzle path is unchanged.  qsa_decode_attn_set_vbatch overrides the environment (for the parity test).

Default (switch off): unchanged.  Checked on sm_86 (CUDA 12, Release): cuobjdump -sass of all 17
existing kernels in qsa_decode_attn.cu.o (attn_chunk_kernel<M>, <M, true>, attn_chunk_slots_kernel
<M, false/true>, attn_merge_kernel) is identical instruction for instruction, control words included,
and the registers are unchanged (37-63).  The new kernels: 8 cells 60-68 registers, 4 cells 43-63,
no spills except 4 bytes in the lane-cell K8V4 one at 8 cells.  Their value loop issues the group's
LDGs together, then 96 (48) FFMA, with the scalar loop's I2F/HADD2.F32/FMUL per cell.  Not run on a
GPU yet; qsa_vbatch_parity (next commit) compares off against 8 and 4.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
